    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 28th February 2006, the erection of a roof extension measuring a 3.8m projection, a height of 2.4m and a width of 4.8m, was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development falls within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995.\r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - Informatives\r\n\r\n1) No part of the proposed rear roof extension may exceed the height of the highest part of the existing roof.\r\n\r\n2) The roof light to be located within the front roof slope of the dwellinghouse shall be flush with that roof plane.\r\n"
